<title>NORWAY: Oil loadings resumed at Statfjord, Gullfaks fields.</title>
<headline>Oil loadings resumed at Statfjord, Gullfaks fields.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crude loadings at the North Sea Statfjord and Gullfaks developments resumed early on Thursday and both fields were running at full production, operator Den norske stats oljeselskap AS said.</p>
<p>&quot;All production is normal. Loadings resumed during the night,&quot; a Statoil spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Loadings were halted on Wednesday because of high waves, but production was kept up because both fields have huge storage tanks.</p>
<p>Crude loadings at offshore buoys are often disrupted during the winter months because of bad weather. Tankers cannot load when waves run higher than about four metres.</p>
<p>--Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
